{
  "$comment": "N-12: THE Dock ×4 (web packages/ui dock.tsx + agent-session.tsx + the chat route, desktop crates/ui dock.rs + steer_viewer.rs + session_chat.rs, iOS ExpUI Dock.swift + AgentSessionView.swift + the UI/Chat screen, Android ui/components/Dock.kt + AgentSessionScreen.kt + the ui/chat screen; models desktop domain::dock, iOS ExpCore Dock.swift, Android domain/Dock.kt). The transcript is the ONE scroll region of a session and a chat, header to the Dock band's top edge; the Dock is the band UNDER it in the composer column (#EXP-1782, Danny: the transcript's scroll area ENDS at the band's top edge, the composer's when no card waits; its content is clipped there, nothing renders below or behind the band, no edge fade, no gradient, no shadow on the band or the composer; pinned to the newest row, the last row sits fully visible just above it): the DockCards, `stack.gap` apart when fanned, then THE composer (always; it never yields its slot, N-12 retires `composerYieldsToCard`). The band's measured height is where the transcript's scroll area ends (a growing band shrinks it and a pinned transcript re-pins to its newest row) and the jump-to-bottom offset. A DockCard = the AskCard chrome (`icons`/tint per `kind`, the tinted `label`, the muted `caption`, the trailing muted `meta`) over ONE `title` line and the `open` chevron (`expandable`) or the banner's `action` word; one height per row. SEVERAL cards pile like the toasts (toast-stack.json, `stackLayout` of src/stack.ts with THIS file's `stack`, anchored at the bottom): the front card is the LAST row, the older ones peek out ABOVE it by `stack.peek` and shrink by `stack.scaleStep` per rank, `stack.visible` of them at most (`hidden` = the rest); a pointer hovering the pile or a tap on it FANS it (every card at full size `stack.gap` apart, mode `fanned`); leaving or tapping the pile again re-piles. A tap (pointer: a click) on a card OPENS it: THE bottom sheet (`sheet`): a scrim, the sheet in the composer column on wide screens (`sheet.radius` on its top corners) and edge to edge on phones (the grabber, drag to dismiss), fitting its content up to `sheet.maxHeightFraction` of the viewport; a pinned HEADER (the card's icon, label, caption, the host's meta, trailing `copy.close` as a ghost icon-xs button), ONE scrolling body, a pinned FOOTER for the primary actions; Escape, the scrim, the close glyph or a drag closes it; it slides up with motion `sheet` (slow decelerate in, standard accelerate out; reduce motion = a fade), the pile moves over `motion.pile` with the standard easing, a card enters with `motion.enter` (decelerate) and leaves over `motion.exit` (accelerate). Rows = `dockRows(sources)`, ordered `order` first (queued, tasks, suggestions, banner, then the asks oldest first by createdAt, ties by id) so the card needing the viewer is in front: `plan` (label ask-dock `planReady`, caption = the asking session's name, meta = `copy.questions` when it has any, title = the plan's first plain line, ask-dock `askDockTitle`), `question` (label ask-dock `question`), `tasks` (THE Queue of task-queue.json: label = the todo title, caption = the completed title, title = the first todo item, meta = its description; opens the full Trace), `queued` (label `copy.queued`, title = the oldest queued message; opens the list with its remove glyphs), `suggestions` (EXP-1323's suggested-tasks card while ANY item is open: label = the header's count (`3 suggested tasks`), caption = its `started` part or null, title = the first open item's title; opens the list: an open item = its title and text, the Start button and the ⋯ menu (Do it here · Start on… · Start with… · File as issue · Dismiss), a started item = the child's session card, here/filed = their one line; the footer = Start all while more than one item is open; a row with no open item stays in the Conversation), `banner` (a status strip of the session view: S-3 no paused strip ×4 (an offline host is invisible); connection lost, the usage wall, compacting, the rate-limit window, starting; the host's `icon`, `label`, `text` and tone `muted`|`warning`; `action` = its one button word; never expandable). ONE GRAY ×4 (owner 2026-10-22): every card on the band and in the transcript, the composer and the sheet wear the same opaque card fill (the design tokens' `card` composite, web `bg-glass-card-opaque`) under the card hairline; nothing translucent, no second tone. `dock({rows, expanded, openId})` = the view: `mode` none|single|pile|fanned, `rows` top to bottom, `frontId`, `openId` (null unless that row exists and is expandable), `hidden`. AUTO-OPEN: `dockAutoOpen({previous, rows})` = the id of the front-most plan or question NOT in `previous` (the ids seen so far), else null; a host opens that sheet when the view is IN FRONT (visible, the session or chat open) and leaves a card that arrived while away collapsed. The host SEEDS `previous` with every card it shows until its data has loaded (the session view: the relay is live, its history replayed; the chat: its rows arrived) and for `autoOpenGraceMs` after that, so what already waited when the view opened never opens itself; only a card arriving after that does. The relay's own asks (claude's AskUserQuestion) are `question` sources too. Answered cards stay in the transcript, closed. Model = pure `dockRows`, `dock`, `dockAutoOpen` (src/dock.ts); mirrors compare the WHOLE expected object. S-3 (owner 2026-10-28): a waiting plan or question is not a DockCard: a plan is the chat's Plan tab (plan-page.json), and both are listed in Needs you (needs-you.json). Hosts pass no `plan`/`question` source any more, the relay's own engine ask (AskUserQuestion / ExitPlanMode) included: that ask stays inline at its place in the feed (FEED-140), answerable with its hotkeys. The Dock keeps tasks, queued, suggestions and banner. Those kinds stay in the model and in these cases for old data, and `dockAutoOpen` has nothing to open. The card itself still draws INLINE in the transcript, answerable (ask-dock.json). LOCAL FIRST (#EXP-1538): the Dock draws in the first frame of the view from what the host already holds, never after the stream connects: the synced sources (the server queue, the session banner, the usage wall, the agent hint) never wait on the stream, and the stream's latest-wins slots (THE Queue's task_list + background_tasks, the relay queue, compaction, the rate limit) show the LAST-KNOWN value for that session (the per-session relay store outlives the screen) while the stream is connecting, reconnecting or parked, until the live replay restates them in one commit; a session that is over (ended) shows none of them. A card present when the view opens enters like any other, with `motion.enter`: opacity 0 to 1 while rising `stack.gap` into its place, decelerate (reduce motion = the fade only), never a late pop; the band's height follows its cards with `motion.pile` from the first frame they are measured. CHAT QUEUE (#EXP-1545): a chat's Dock shows at most ONE `tasks` card, from ONE session of its tree: the ROOT's while the root is not ended and its Queue is open (a todo item to show), else the most recently active LIVE child's (not ended, its Queue open; most recent = the latest `lastTurnAt`, else `startedAt`, none = oldest; ties by id ascending), else none. `chatDockQueue(candidates)` = `{sessionId, sessionName}` (sessionName null for the root, else the child's name) or null; a candidate = `{sessionId, name, root, ended, activeAt, open}`. The host reads each Live child's per-session relay slots like the root's (LOCAL FIRST: the last-known value while its stream connects; an ended session contributes nothing) and passes the chosen session's Queue as the `tasks` source with its `sessionName`: caption = `sessionName · completed title` (either alone when the other is missing, null when both are); the card's sheet opens THAT session's Trace. Every other kind (queued, banners, suggestions) stays the root's. The session view passes no `sessionName` (absent = null). ONE CHILD STREAM (#EXP-1623 on iOS, #EXP-1678 ×4): the chat never opens a stream per Live child (#EXP-1545 did: one phone dialled every child of a chat at once, 4 to 9 joins to ONE device over its one ordered eNet stream, and the views failed to settle in bursts). It holds at most ONE child stream, on the child `chatQueueProbe(rootOpen, children)` names: none while the root's own Queue is open; else the children in `chatDockQueue`'s order (latest activeAt first, none = oldest, ties by id ascending) and the first whose state is not `closed` (an `open` one is the pick itself, an `unknown` one is read next); every child closed = none. A child's state (`chatQueueChildState`, cases `childStateCases`): `open` when its stream (attached, or one this install already holds) has a todo item; else `closed` when a read of it is REMEMBERED closed (same activeAt, within `closedQueueTtlMs` of the read: a child that turns again, or the TTL, re-reads it); else, with a stream, `closed` when that stream is `starting` (no device feeds it), `closed` (dropped), `ended`, has REPLAYED without an open Queue, or has been attached `probeDeadlineMs` without either; else `unknown`. A child read `closed` is remembered (keyed by its activeAt) and its stream released; the next in line is read. The chat re-evaluates the probe when the root's Queue, a child's activeAt or a state changes, and once `probeDeadlineMs` after each attach. `chatQueueProbeCases`: {rootOpen, children [{sessionId, activeAt, state}]} -> expected (sessionId | null). `childStateCases`: {open, remembered, stream (null | {phase: connecting | live | starting | closed | ended, replayed, attachedMs})} -> state.",
